herdbook-tabs is a modified copy of the `tabs` mod shipped with the Herdr
desktop app 0.1.16 (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app), licensed under
the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE in this folder).

Changes from the original: a tab with several panes on screen lists each
pane's icon and name (`pane-name` label, Herdr 0.1.17+ `pane.name`, or Herdr's
label), and each segment can be dragged out on its own (to the blank tab-bar
space, another tab's edges, or another tab's center to join); a tab someone
named shows all icons (each draggable) and its name, and dragging a single-pane
tab onto another tab's center merges them. Naming and drop-zone helpers live in
names.js, and drag.js provides native + pure-JS cross-panel drag. A right-click
opens herdbook-menu and + opens launch-menu when installed. With any visible
sibling block after it in a row (such as `frost` or `usage-meter` in
`tabs-row`), right padding tightens to 3px instead of 10px. Asset paths were
renamed by Herdr's mod.clone.
